# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.13.1 - Monitor and control communications at boundaries
# Platform: M365 (Entra ID)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against CA policies for legacy-auth blocking

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-13-1-m365-comm-boundary-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `high`

    title `CMMC L1 SC.L1-3.13.1: Monitor and control communications at external boundaries`
    description `Validates that at least one enabled Conditional Access policy blocks legacy authentication protocols. Legacy auth bypasses Conditional Access altogether and is a primary external-boundary risk; explicitly blocking it satisfies the practice of controlling communications at the boundary.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-13-1,sc,communications-boundary,legacy-auth`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.13.1`
    control_objective `3.13.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:identity-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Configure at least one enabled Conditional Access policy with conditions.clientAppTypes including legacy protocols (exchangeActiveSync, other) and a grant control of block. This ensures legacy authentication, which bypasses modern security controls, cannot reach tenant resources from the external boundary.`

    component_id `comp-m365-identity`

    impl_3_13_1 `Organizational communications are controlled at the external boundary by Conditional Access policies that block legacy authentication protocols. Modern authentication protocols are subject to multi-factor and conditional-access evaluation; legacy protocols bypass these controls. By explicitly blocking legacy authentication, all incoming communication is forced through the modern authentication pipeline where boundary-monitoring controls apply. Server-side enforcement at the identity provider ensures the block is effective regardless of client behavior.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT enabled_ca_policies
        path `identity/conditionalAccess/policies`
        filter `state eq 'enabled'`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE blocks_legacy_auth
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.conditions.clientAppTypes.* string = `exchangeActiveSync` at_least_one
            field rows.*.grantControls.builtInControls.* string = `block` at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF blocks_legacy_auth
            OBJECT_REF enabled_ca_policies
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
